<div id="2026-09-05-helpdesk-staff-display-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-05 — Confirm HelpDesk landing uses is_staff (admin OR helpdesk); clean remaining hard-coded checks</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Verified that CSC/HelpDesk.tt landing staff card uses <code>[% IF is_staff %]</code> (populated by controller _is_staff which accepts 'admin' || 'helpdesk'). No TT-level restriction to only 'admin'. Added JS config injection for client isAdmin/isStaff/roleTier. Fixed last hard-coded <code>c.check_user_roles('admin')</code> badge in ticket_status.tt (now uses stashed is_staff || is_admin_view and "Staff View" label). Updated _load_admin_tickets is_csc logic and ticket_list stash to include is_admin_view for helpdesk role. </p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Landing was still showing member-only cards on :4009 because running process had not picked up .pm changes that stash is_staff in index (and added queue/staff actions). /ticket/list title and some views relied on controller vars sourced from _is_staff but templates had one leftover strict admin check.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/root/CSC/HelpDesk.tt</code> (JS block), <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/HelpDesk.pm</code> (ticket_list stash, _load_admin_tickets is_csc), <code>Comserv/root/CSC/HelpDesk/ticket_status.tt</code> (badge conditional), <code>Comserv/root/Documentation/changelog/entries/2026-09-05-helpdesk-staff-display-fix.inc</code></p>
</div>